    "narrative": "The premier play for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Mickey Moniak**, who carries a dominant 75.97 score into his matchup against Roki Sasaki. While the opposing starter is formidable, the intersection of an elite hitter\u2019s park and **Mickey Moniak**\u2019s favorable platoon split creates a massive efficiency ceiling; furthermore, Sasaki\u2019s slow delivery to the plate creates a premium opportunity for him to exploit the base paths\u2014a critical edge given our internal focus on SB scarcity. **Isaac Paredes** (64.30) also emerges as a high-floor anchor, benefiting significantly from a favorable platoon advantage and a middle-of-the-order slot that should maximize his counting stat production against Ure\u00f1a. Conversely, **Seiya Suzuki** (58.53) remains a strong start, as the park factors and his lineup position help him comfortably weather a sub-optimal matchup against Newcomb.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision centered on **Austin Riley** (54.14), who sits on the bench despite a respectable projection. While he benefited from an elite base-stealing environment against Bradley\u2019s delivery, the combination of a lower-tier batting order position and higher-upside efficiency from **Josh Naylor** (60.48) and **Max Muncy** (56.10) pushed him just below the threshold. We are monitoring the status of **Max Muncy** and **Brice Turang** closely; as their lineups are currently pending, a shift in order could further compress their efficiency scores. We must also exercise caution with **Corbin Carroll** and **Griffin Conine**; despite their talent, both are facing elite hold pitchers in Tolle and Nola, which severely limits the probability of successful stolen base attempts\u2014a key component of our strategic weightings today.",
